# Notes and mail


::divider{wavy|Notes and mail|green}
## Waterflow

#C#Notes#= [Open Waterflow](/waterflow)

A clear, glassy notebook. Notes live in #R.marker(streams), #R.marker(notebooks) and #R.marker(tags), and are written in Poolside Keydown!

* #GL.flag(Quick switcher): press Ctrl+K to jump to any note!
* #Y.flag(Three modes): View, Visual and Source, like Writeout!
* #L.flag(Outline) of the headings, and a #R.marker(trash) you can restore from!
* #G.flag(More): wiki links between notes, templates, tasks, a calendar, history, a writing goal, statistics, quick capture and a typewriter mode!
* #TU.flag(Waterflow Legacy) keeps the original app, and the new Waterflow can bring its notes over!

## Yuzu

#B#Mail#= [Open Yuzu](/yuzu) · [Phone version](/yuzu/mobile/)

An email app with an inbox, folders, search and compose. It has two looks: a new Outlook-style ribbon, and the original #G.marker(Yuzu Classic)!

### Accounts

* #G.accent(A Yuzu address) (`name@radii-office.com`) that you make inside the app!
* #TU.accent(Google or Microsoft accounts), which use the provider's own sign-in. The sign-in needs the app's client ID to be set up in the app's settings!

### Keydown in messages

Messages you write are Keydown, so headings, chips and styles work. When you send to another Yuzu address, the message arrives with its Keydown and is drawn in full!

### Mail from the outside world

Mail from other services often has its own formatting. Yuzu shows the #G.marker(formatted version) in a sandboxed frame:

* Scripts never run, and links open in a new tab!
* Pictures from the internet are #G.marker(blocked) until you press #G.marker(Load pictures)!
* #G.spotlight(Plain text) is one click away on every message!

Mail is kept in memory for Google and Microsoft accounts and is not stored by the app. Mail sent to a Yuzu address is stored on the Yuzu mail server until you delete it!

## Trigger

See [Trigger](#/trigger) for rules that react when your documents change!
